From 78d1541428a70a8d5b708636c6d42368522acc31 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 04:19:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Config: hypre on the host, request read before the
 initialization of hypre

Review of the previous commit:

- the request of hypre on the host (options and MFEM_MGIS_HYPRE_ON_HOST,
  getHypreOnHostRequest) is read by initialize before mfem::Hypre::Init,
  so that mfem::Hypre::configure_runtime_policy_from_mfem is false when
  hypre is initialized: a device configured before (by the program or by
  the variable MFEM_DEVICE of MFEM) no longer makes hypre use the GPU and
  initialize its libraries on the GPU before the policy is set back to
  the host. The previous commit stated that each of the two settings was
  sufficient with hypre 3.2, whose default policy would be the host: this
  was an effect of the order of the calls (mfem::Hypre::Init had already
  set the host, the device not being configured yet). hypre built with
  GPU support computes on the GPU by default: both settings are needed,
  and removing either of them makes tests fail;
- with hypre built with GPU support and older than 2.31, the request
  given by the environment variable is ignored with a warning, as the
  other variables of initialize;
- documentation: PETSc may make hypre use the GPU again (conversion of
  its matrices located on a GPU), the short cancelling option, the
  accepted values of the variable, the refusal of ParaSails when hypre
  computes on the GPU.

Tests: RESOURCE_LOCK gpu for BatchIntegrationTestP-cuda-hypre-on-host;
DeviceOptionTest creates a device after the initialization with
--create-device, accepts any memory of the host with
--expected-host-memory any, and expects hypre on the device only if
hypre may compute on a GPU; new variants with the device configured by
MFEM_DEVICE or by the program, with and without --hypre-on-host.
